From dc6e2ca2fae29b0c0e76659deb30f54be07a7e88 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Manuel Kuklinski <mk@asdfghasdfgh.de>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 09:04:21 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] ath79: add Zyxel NWA5123-AC support

Add the zyxel-deadbeaf builders and the NWA5123-AC device definition.
ZLD only writes section data to flash, so section 0 carries the OKLI
loader stub in the kernel partition and section 1 carries the OKLI
kernel plus squashfs rootfs in the zldfs partition, padded with 0xFF
to the full partition size so the jffs2 overlay starts clean.

The loader probes the CS0 image slot first and falls back to reading
CS1 via SPI at the zldfs offset. Add a first-boot script that mirrors
the OKLI stub into both Zyxel image slots so ZLD boots OpenWrt
regardless of its persistent bootImage flag, and document the flash
layout, boot flow, installation, recovery, Ethernet tuning, mesh and
802.11r setup.
